.TH JWALK 1
.SH NAME
jwalk \\- walk directory trees with structured filters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jwalk
jwalk [--format json|ndjson] [--include REGEX] [--exclude REGEX] [--type LIST]
.br
[--min-size SIZE] [--max-size SIZE] [--older-than DURATION] [--newer-than DURATION]
.br
[--follow-symlinks] [--fail-on-error] ROOT ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Emits JSON or NDJSON records for matching filesystem entries. Filters include regex, type, size, age, symlink handling, and error policy.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBjwalk --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
